{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"6e04d9643b6f2c4ad3c1e13730299dc36c2f43decced29f870399e7adabbec8c","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've traced the issue: the ground map clears grass across the whole pond radius whenever terrain sits within 45 cm of the water, and since this crater's rim is only ~30 cm above the waterline, the entire bowl gets wiped into a hard circle instead of following the shoreline. I'll let grass grow in to within a few centimetres of the water so the edge matches the actual shoreline.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BBA6jZNyht9JvNEF3coguY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np='js/groundmap.js'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"  // nor in the water standing in the craters (ponds.js)\n  for (const p of ponds || []) {\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"  // nor in the water standing in the craters (ponds.js), the grass growing down to a few\n  // centimetres above it (a crater is shallow: kept off the whole bowl, its edge was the\n  // cut-off circle's, not the water's)\n  for (const p of ponds || []) {\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nold=\"\"\"      const keep = smoothstep(0.1, 0.45, H[k] - p.y);\n      for (let c = 0; c < 3; c++) cov[k * 3 + c] *= keep;\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"      const keep = smoothstep(0.03, 0.16, H[k] - p.y);\n      for (let c = 0; c < 3; c++) cov[k * 3 + c] *= keep;\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"tSward\\|swardMap\\|createSward\\|sward\" js/*.js | grep -v \"^js/terrain.js\" | head","description":"Let grass grow down to the pond waterline"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
