{"parentUuid":"cb188e9c-4cc1-4763-b42d-9b884de186f6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6d5c0a1d-fdd5-4db0-8cbd-a5c82a0adcb7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019MrGG3MDW1SBCssQmtRsBi","type":"tool_result","content":"renderer adds wet ground — dark, glossy cobbles with water in the joints\n(and, near the eye, real depth: the stones stand proud of their joints, the\nmud keeps its ruts, the march of the view ray through the height maps),\npuddles with soaked margins in the hollows that mirror the lit windows, the\nlamps and the glow of the sky, broken by rain rings, river banks soaked\nabove the waterline with a thin broken line of scum where the water laps\nthem and the water browner in the shallows of the ford, a forest floor of last year's leaves with moss in the\ndamp, leaves and litter in the gutters, brick bits round the shelled houses,\nstones and fallen branches along the lane and the forest track, whose mud is\ncut by two wheel ruts with a grassy crown between them and water standing in\nthem in stretches, rainwater standing in the shell craters — rain in fine\n    distance across and along them, from which the terrain cuts two ruts a\n    cart's track apart, wandering a little, into its near-eye relief, dark\n    with wet mud, holding water in stretches, a grassy crown between them\n  * `ponds.js` rainwater in the shell craters (the level's `craters`): a\n    disc at two fifths of each holding bowl's depth, cut by the bowl's own\n    sides, drawn with the river's water held still (shallows and a line of\n    scum from its depth in the ground map, rain rings, no white glint of the\n    night's fill light); the ground map keeps grass and clutter out of it\n  * `groundmap.js` what grows and lies where, made at load from the\n    terrain mesh's own splat: grass, stones and fallen wood (none on roads,\n    steep banks, at the water or inside anything solid), and the ground's\n38:renderer adds wet ground — dark, glossy cobbles with water in the joints\n43:above the waterline with a thin broken line of scum where the water laps\n44:them and the water browner in the shallows of the ford, a forest floor of last year's leaves with moss in the\n47:cut by two wheel ruts with a grassy crown between them and water standing in\n48:them in stretches, rainwater standing in the shell craters — rain in fine\n148:    with wet mud, holding water in stretches, a grassy crown between them\n149:  * `ponds.js` rainwater in the shell craters (the level's `craters`): a\n151:    sides, drawn with the river's water held still (shallows and a line of\n156:    steep banks, at the water or inside anything solid), and the ground's\n169:    mottling everything and roughening what is baked rough, not where water\n199:    water off the eaves: at load the lower edges of the roofs are found in\n202:    each fall is one thin ribbon whose shader places the falling water on","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a67582e7-83a8-49fd-b137-a8019f0fb276","timestamp":"2026-10-21T22:14:25.021Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"renderer adds wet ground — dark, glossy cobbles with water in the joints\n(and, near the eye, real depth: the stones stand proud of their joints, the\nmud keeps its ruts, the march of the view ray through the height maps),\npuddles with soaked margins in the hollows that mirror the lit windows, the\nlamps and the glow of the sky, broken by rain rings, river banks soaked\nabove the waterline with a thin broken line of scum where the water laps\nthem and the water browner in the shallows of the ford, a forest floor of last year's leaves with moss in the\ndamp, leaves and litter in the gutters, brick bits round the shelled houses,\nstones and fallen branches along the lane and the forest track, whose mud is\ncut by two wheel ruts with a grassy crown between them and water standing in\nthem in stretches, rainwater standing in the shell craters — rain in fine\n    distance across and along them, from which the terrain cuts two ruts a\n    cart's track apart, wandering a little, into its near-eye relief, dark\n    with wet mud, holding water in stretches, a grassy crown between them\n  * `ponds.js` rainwater in the shell craters (the level's `craters`): a\n    disc at two fifths of each holding bowl's depth, cut by the bowl's own\n    sides, drawn with the river's water held still (shallows and a line of\n    scum from its depth in the ground map, rain rings, no white glint of the\n    night's fill light); the ground map keeps grass and clutter out of it\n  * `groundmap.js` what grows and lies where, made at load from the\n    terrain mesh's own splat: grass, stones and fallen wood (none on roads,\n    steep banks, at the water or inside anything solid), and the ground's\n38:renderer adds wet ground — dark, glossy cobbles with water in the joints\n43:above the waterline with a thin broken line of scum where the water laps\n44:them and the water browner in the shallows of the ford, a forest floor of last year's leaves with moss in the\n47:cut by two wheel ruts with a grassy crown between them and water standing in\n48:them in stretches, rainwater standing in the shell craters — rain in fine\n148:    with wet mud, holding water in stretches, a grassy crown between them\n149:  * `ponds.js` rainwater in the shell craters (the level's `craters`): a\n151:    sides, drawn with the river's water held still (shallows and a line of\n156:    steep banks, at the water or inside anything solid), and the ground's\n169:    mottling everything and roughening what is baked rough, not where water\n199:    water off the eaves: at load the lower edges of the roofs are found in\n202:    each fall is one thin ribbon whose shader places the falling water on","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"cb46a9ea-032e-41c4-8a78-b43d58edaef8","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hed