{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"767b4d9bc5b1341d1e6e5899c6658b010d4f8785c1071d53d3961c5fc50fe921","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The diff reads correctly. Committing."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SsnosKjqAN8QMobK3CxpUc","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git add fun/hedgerow/README.md fun/hedgerow/js/groundmap.js fun/hedgerow/js/levelBuild.js fun/hedgerow/js/materials.js fun/hedgerow/js/ssr.js fun/hedgerow/js/terrain.js && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: rain on the water at the scale of raindrops\n\nThe river borrowed the rock texture's normal map for its waves, and its\nstraight cracks showed as a lattice of creases across the water. It now\nhas long low swells drawn out along the current with a finer chop over\nthem, carried downstream: three octaves of value noise and its analytic\nslope, the octaves turned against each other so the grid never lines up.\n\nRain rings everywhere (river, ponds, puddles, wet tops, and the\nreflection pass that ruffles its mirror with the same rings) were up to\n1.2 m across and sparse, more fish than rain. They are now small, many\nand quick, and fade out between 8 and 16 m where a ring would be\nsmaller than a pixel. Past that the work is skipped, and the terrain now\nevaluates them only in its puddles. Further off, the rain only roughens\nthe water.\n\nThe crater ponds read as pale-rimmed plates: their scum line was so\nmany centimetres deep, which on a shallow crater's gentle bank spread\ninto a wide pale band. It is now a hand's breadth from the edge\n(depth over the bed's rise, from the ground map) and darker. The ground\nround the craters is drawn at the fine grid, so the water's edge\nfollows the bowl instead of a few metre-wide facets, and the grass\ngrows down to a few centimetres above the water.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1 && git merge-tree --write-tree hedgerow-poc hedgerow-grass >/dev/null && echo \"merge with hedgerow-poc: clean\"","description":"Commit the water changes and check the merge"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
