{"parentUuid":"ae0dc276-7019-4fee-aa29-8153789327ed","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgG9s35V8eysshVL6Jr2p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01M8x6E8G86LxyNfoiZLhYEW","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Library/Application REDACTED.md","old_string":"  placement + ~60 ms painting the break texture at load; GPU within noise (0.1-0.4 ms in the square).\n","new_string":"  placement + ~60 ms painting the break texture at load; GPU within noise (0.1-0.4 ms in the square).\n- 83aa87e4 water: (1) river/pond normals now procedural (3 octaves value noise + analytic slope,\n  vnoiseDW in createWaterMaterial); the old normalMap (textures.rock) put straight crease lines\n  across the river. (2) GLSL_HELPERS rainRipples(p, t, fade) - NEW SIGNATURE (third arg; callers\n  pass rippleFade(viewDistance)), cells now 1/2.4 of the old, rings faster; skipped at fade 0;\n  terrain calls it only where tPuddle > 0.01. (3) pond scum line by distance to the edge (depth /\n  bed slope) and darker (was a wide pale band on shallow craters). (4) levelBuild adds every\n  crater's square to the terrain's `fine` list (+~100k terrain vertices in 30 chunks) so the pond\n  edge is not a coarse polygon. (5) groundmap: grass grows to 3-16 cm above pond water.\n  Frame times unchanged within noise (street 19.1, square 16.3, river 18.3 ms).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1223,"cache_read_input_tokens":578075,"output_tokens":610,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1223,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":610,"cache_read_input_tokens":578075,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1223,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1223},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01M8x6E8G86LxyNfoiZLhYEW":{"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Library/Application REDACTED.md","old_string":"  placement + ~60 ms painting the break texture at load; GPU within noise (0.1-0.4 ms in the square).\n","new_string":"  placement + ~60 ms painting the break texture at load; GPU within noise (0.1-0.4 ms in the square).\n- 83aa87e4 water: (1) river/pond normals now procedural (3 octaves value noise + analytic slope,\n  vnoiseDW in createWaterMaterial); the old normalMap (textures.rock) put straight crease lines\n  across the river. (2) GLSL_HELPERS rainRipples(p, t, fade) - NEW SIGNATURE (third arg; callers\n  pass rippleFade(viewDistance)), cells now 1/2.4 of the old, rings faster; skipped at fade 0;\n  terrain calls it only where tPuddle > 0.01. (3) pond scum line by distance to the edge (depth /\n  bed slope) and darker (was a wide pale band on shallow craters). (4) levelBuild adds every\n  crater's square to the terrain's `fine` list (+~100k terrain vertices in 30 chunks) so the pond\n  edge is not a coarse polygon. (5) groundmap: grass grows to 3-16 cm above pond water.\n  Frame times unchanged within noise (street 19.1, square 16.3, river 18.3 ms).\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a11aa159-13a5-4cdc-8b6e-dfd306122a8e","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgG9s2QpDN8qxVGPXj3NT","requestRef":"1578ef5a-6701-4bbc-aae1-906bfb682036","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"aa7e4492-194d-40f3-a70d-a761fb4085cc","timestamp":"2026-10-21T22:15:07.761Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4f