{"parentUuid":"efb33182-f852-4969-82ac-fe9524903142","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGALvryVQQMEYBQF3tnp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This round added two commits to `hedgerow-grass`, none pushed: 83aa87e4 and e6668e1b. Node checks pass, shaders compile on low, medium and high, and the merge with `hedgerow-poc` is still clean.\n\n- **83aa87e4 – rain on the water at the scale of raindrops**\n  - **River creases:** straight lines crossed the whole river surface. The water was using the rock texture's normal map, whose cracks showed through. It now has procedural swells stretched along the current, with finer ripples carried downstream.\n  - **Rain rings:** they were up to 1.2 m across and sparse, looking more like fish than rain. Now they're small, dense and quick, on the river, ponds, puddles and in reflections alike. Beyond 16 m they're skipped, since they'd be smaller than a pixel; there the rain just roughens the water a little.\n  - **Crater ponds:** they looked like flat plates with a pale rim. The scum line is now a thin dark line at the water's edge. The ground around craters uses the finer terrain grid, so the water's edge follows the bowl instead of a coarse polygon. Grass grows down to just above the water.\n  - Frame times are unchanged within noise (street 19.1 ms, square 16.3 ms, river 18.3 ms).\n- **e6668e1b – undergrowth that sits in the shade**\n  - The ferns were the brightest thing in the forest: flat, saturated green on a near-black floor. Every leaf got the same extra glow, so dense ground plants lit up like the sunlit edge of a tree crown. That glow now follows how thin the foliage is.\n  - Every tree and plant now has a slightly different green, with an occasional one turning yellow-brown. Each tree keeps the same tint at every distance, so nothing pops when its model switches.\n  - The ground-plant colours are a little duller. A stronger version made the meadow's grass clumps disappear, so I backed it off.\n\nAll test servers are stopped, no browser tabs are open, and my `launch.json` entry is removed. Notes are in the shared notes file; the main one for other work is that the rain-ring shader function now takes a third argument."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":294,"cache_read_input_tokens":622145,"output_tokens":716,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":294,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":716,"cache_read_input_tokens":622145,"cache_creation_input_tokens":294,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":294},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d100176b-5fa5-4bc5-a230-0f2748b88eb6","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgGALuuv9jcqyLRgJeime","requestRef":"4bd2cc13-c5ff-4627-9e49-765f3569ed49","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"6db2f2d7-c1eb-4c7e-aa4a-3ff827c1e50d","timestamp":"2026-10-21T22:21:26.871Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"REDACTED","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
