{"parentUuid":"fabdc05a-74a7-4d72-8164-00444c12e913","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGBTKazXtdfLXYHiEZ4X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This round added two commits to `hedgerow-grass`, none pushed: 2c7f3751 and 9c7ccef6. Node checks pass, the high-quality shaders compile, and the merge with `hedgerow-poc` is still clean.\n\n- **2c7f3751 – rounds through the hedges shred their leaves.** A bullet into a hedge or bush used to throw generic dirt chunks that dropped like stones. In a mission fought across hedgerows, that's most misses.\n  - Now it bursts 16–24 leaf scraps out of the hedge that flutter down, eddy and drift downwind for a few seconds, with green dust, a twig or two, and rain shaken off the leaves.\n  - Enemy misses now carry their direction to the impact, as the player's already did.\n  - A six-second stress test at 20 hits a second levelled off at about 1050 live particles out of 3000, and the burst thins out when the pool gets busy.\n- **9c7ccef6 – muzzle flashes with a shape and a colour.** An enemy machine gun firing at you from a few metres read as a white ball.\n  - Now it's a smaller white-hot star inside two ragged orange tongues of flame, different every shot, with a few sparks of burning powder flying ahead.\n  - The player's own shots get the same treatment.\n  - I tried two other outer layers and dropped them: a soft glow looked like an orange orb, and a second star just added more spikes.\n\nI reviewed and left alone:\n- **Trench floor:** it renders almost black, but it's wet mud under the night sky, so an exposure matter rather than a defect.\n- **Floating pale discs:** the ones near the ground are mist puffs, not an artifact.\n\nOne thing needs your decision: at night in the forest, enemies about 18 m away are nearly invisible, dark uniforms against dark woods, even when they're in clear view. That's realistic, but it's a difficulty and readability call, so I haven't changed it. Making them more visible would mean adding a subtle rim or sheen to the soldiers.\n\nAll test servers are stopped, no browser tabs are open, and my `launch.json` entry is removed. Notes are in the shared notes file."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":260,"cache_read_input_tokens":728438,"output_tokens":718,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":260,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":718,"cache_read_input_tokens":728438,"cache_creation_input_tokens":260,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":260},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"3e88be18-2a76-4d6a-a52d-3b7aa476ab99","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgGBTJvYj6Gn4o8eoLcTX","requestRef":"a4bcedff-c433-4f72-b2be-fad85b8351db","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"03ac7ab8-6480-43b9-a113-07f3f24c7b61","timestamp":"2026-10-21T22:36:00.612Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"REDACTED","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
