{"parentUuid":"6d2b7f70-fb51-41ee-a6a7-3d09f0d1b3e8","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01GFT1Wi1XBi6dengj9i9Rnu","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"23346be5-db75-44c7-96aa-55840702a630","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:00:48.143Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"23346be5-db75-44c7-96aa-55840702a630","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGDLwL6GE5DKPaw1owFk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PrYMo3jEZ4AXV7xvAxE7fW","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np='fun/hedgerow/README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"    and beyond them, out to ~60 m, sheets of rain worked out per pixel on\n    four cylinders round the eye in one full-screen draw, hidden behind the\n    scene by its depth, lit by the lamps near them and by a burning flare;\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"    and beyond them, out to ~60 m, sheets of rain worked out per pixel on\n    four cylinders round the eye in one full-screen draw, hidden behind the\n    scene by its depth (on low quality, which has no depth to read, the same\n    four cylinders drawn as meshes with the scene, hidden by its depth test),\n    lit by the lamps near them and by a burning flare;\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit add fun/hedgerow/README.md fun/hedgerow/js/weather.js && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: rain on low quality too\n\nOn the low preset it hardly rained. The rain sheets that carry the\nlook of a downpour (four cylinders of streaks out to 60 m) need the\nlate pass's depth texture to hide behind the scene, which low quality\ndoes not have, so they were off. The near streaks alone, tuned to sit\nunder the sheets, were all but invisible even at nine times their\nopacity.\n\nThe sheets' streak and lighting are now one shared GLSL function, used\nby the full-screen draw on medium and high (unchanged) and on low by\nfour open cylinder meshes around the camera, drawn with the scene.\nEach cylinder is depth-tested by the GPU, so the rain hides behind\nthe fountain, the walls and the ground as on high. The pixel scale\ncomes from the real drawing buffer. Cost on the test GPU is within\nnoise (-0.1 to +0.2 ms).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1 && git merge-tree --write-tree hedgerow-poc hedgerow-grass >/dev/null && echo \"merge with hedgerow-poc: clean\"","description":"Commit the low-quality rain and check the merge"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":319,"cache_read_input_tokens":633210,"output_tokens":859,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":319,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":859,"cache_read_input_tokens":633210,"cache_creation_input_tokens":319,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":319},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01PrYMo3jEZ4AXV7xvAxE7fW":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np='fun/hedgerow/README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"    and beyond them, out to ~60 m, sheets of rain worked out per pixel on\n    four cylinders round the eye in one full-screen draw, hidden behind the\n    scene by its depth, lit by the lamps near them and by a burning flare;\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"    and beyond them, out to ~60 m, sheets of rain worked out per pixel on\n    four cylinders round the eye in one full-screen draw, hidden behind the\n    scene by its depth (on low quality, which has no depth to read, the same\n    four cylinders drawn as meshes with the scene, hidden by its depth test),\n    lit by the lamps near them and by a burning flare;\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit add fun/hedgerow/README.md fun/hedgerow/js/weather.js && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: rain on low quality too\n\nOn the low preset it hardly rained. The rain sheets that carry the\nlook of a downpour (four cylinders of streaks out to 60 m) need the\nlate pass's depth texture to hide behind the scene, which low quality\ndoes not have, so they were off. The near streaks alone, tuned to sit\nunder the sheets, were all but invisible even at nine times their\nopacity.\n\nThe sheets' streak and lighting are now one shared GLSL function, used\nby the full-screen draw on medium and high (unchanged) and on low by\nfour open cylinder meshes around the camera, drawn with the scene.\nEach cylinder is depth-tested by the GPU, so the rain hides behind\nthe fountain, the walls and the ground as on high. The pixel scale\ncomes from the real drawing buffer. Cost on the test GPU is within\nnoise (-0.1 to +0.2 ms).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1 && git merge-tree --write-tree hedgerow-poc hedgerow-grass >/dev/null && echo \"merge with hedgerow-poc: clean\"","description":"Commit the low-quality rain and check the merge"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01PrYMo3jEZ4AXV7xvAxE7fW":{"cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"c57f8e43-6638-4714-8a0f-e9ccab815852","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgGDLvZDYe84SyLydLRCX","requestRef":"a7723ec2-48c2-49b9-b065-873194e84dfa","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"9112971d-f116-44c2-a987-7b140632a458","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:00:48.142Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
